{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel","id":232426,"title":"GenCon panel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-17T22:02:35-07:00","id":232426,"title":"GenCon panel","content":"Anyone want to bring us up to speed on Saturday's GenCon panel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:29:40-07:00","id":233619,"title":"","content":"Hoo boy.<br /> <br /> - Scion and Trinity use the same system. Attribute + Ability, d10s. It's based off a modern action system, though it has to scale from man on the street to god in the sky. Dice pools always represent what you're doing, but their Goals and what the roll represents may vary wildly depending on who and what you are.<br /> - Purviews are somewhat reminiscent of Professional Training from God-Machine and Backgrounds, but more holistic and deeply integrated within the system. They're <i>what you are</i> - a cop, a soldier, a writer, an investigator, a therianthrope, a kami. They allow you to access resources thematically and reasonably appropriate to the character, and provide distinct benefits (which can be broad or specific, depending on how specific the Purview gets). The book covers very broad Purviews, but specific ones tailored to an organization aren't out of the question, and GMs are encouraged to create their own - we provide them as template examples, not shackles. Supernatural Purviews also scale upwards, granting access to powers reasonably appropriate to the power set.<br /> - There are three individual scaling mechanisms - Tiers (and no, I didn't explain what they were), Attributes, <b>(other thing). </b>There's also an environmental scaling mechanism; DaveB likened it to Batman being street-level in his own comics while still fighting cosmic aliens with the Justice League. In some settings, a god may be all-powerful in their Godrealm but &quot;merely&quot; a strong and capable mortal in the place furthest divorced from their themes.<br /> - Legend has certain themes according to the dot rating, which may be &quot;mantled&quot; by the god to produce certain divine attributes and power sets. These are acquired by a system of heroic deeds (both in actual play or in an outright character generation). If you're play a Scion, your first dot is always, &quot;Scion of X, God of Y,&quot; which allows you to adopt a lesser set of powers of your parent's most famous mantle. While parentage is clear and may even trace back generations through the Legend system, Scions needn't (and, in fact, it's hard for them) be clones of their parents. Certain relics may be Legend dots, meaning you can't mantle those powers without them.<br /> - <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Zeus, Jupiter and Tinia </span></span>are all the same god, but that god may be mantling different dots of Legend.<br /> - Pantheons are magical constructs within Fate; gods may belong to one or more pantheons. Pantheons are no longer divine bloodlines. Hero talks about what happens to dead gods and shattered pantheons.<br /> <br /> I wish I could talk more about the ten pantheons in Hero (though the core six are back, the Loa are a major subset of the Yoruba), the setting(s) and the fact that you don't <i>have </i>to play a Scion <i>or </i>a mortal, but sadly nobody asked about those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-18-2014, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:26:42-07:00","id":233909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=233619#post233619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish I could talk more about the ten pantheons in Hero (though the core six are back, the Loa are a major subset of the Yoruba), the setting(s) and the fact that you don't <i>have </i>to play a Scion <i>or </i>a mortal, but sadly nobody asked about those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would that mean you'd need authorisation before you could talk about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T01:08:54-07:00","id":233957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=233619#post233619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeus, Jupiter and Tinia are all the same god, but that god may be mantling different dots of Legend</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, this is a brilliant way to deal with <b>that</b> issue. And I love this idea of investing yourself with different &quot;mantles&quot; of power<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dice pools always represent what you're doing, but their Goals and what the roll represents may vary wildly depending on who and what you are. </div> </div> </div>This also seems like a great idea!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T02:42:51-07:00","id":233981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=233619#post233619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hoo boy.<br /> <br /> - Scion and Trinity use the same system. Attribute + Ability, d10s. It's based off a modern action system, though it has to scale from man on the street to god in the sky. Dice pools always represent what you're doing, but their Goals and what the roll represents may vary wildly depending on who and what you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me that sounds like a god would be rolling a similar number of dice as a mortal when attempting to do [a thing] it's just that [a thing] a god tries is more likely to be split Mount Olumpus in twain while a mortal might try to break down a locked door.<br /> <br /> Is it a kind of [things mortals might try with difficulty list] and a [things heroes might try with a difficulty list] and [things demigods might try...etc. And depending on what type of character you are you would perform deeds of your [category] at the associated difficulties?<br /> <br /> Or am I just crazy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=233619#post233619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Purviews are somewhat reminiscent of Professional Training from God-Machine and Backgrounds, but more holistic and deeply integrated within the system. They're <i>what you are</i> - a cop, a soldier, a writer, an investigator, a therianthrope, a kami. They allow you to access resources thematically and reasonably appropriate to the character, and provide distinct benefits (which can be broad or specific, depending on how specific the Purview gets). The book covers very broad Purviews, but specific ones tailored to an organization aren't out of the question, and GMs are encouraged to create their own - we provide them as template examples, not shackles. Supernatural Purviews also scale upwards, granting access to powers reasonably appropriate to the power set.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Purviews are quite narrative then? But also have associated specific powers? Will there be guidance for what kinds of things fall into the Purview of 'a kami' because my knowledge of Japanese myth is pretty limited so I have no idea what would be a suitable thing for 'a kami' to be able to do.<br /> <br /> Can I also ask that, if you've gt the word count, we get a few examples of really specific purviews? Simply because having examples to point to that show explicitly what you have in mind for an 'organisation' as a Purview can really help guide their creation and to aid the GM in knowing what would be suitable for a player to use in game or what kinds of benefits a Purview may offer to an NPC etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T04:06:20-07:00","id":234051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=233909#post233909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would that mean you'd need authorisation before you could talk about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. I'm annoyingly open at Gen Con in that I'll straight up answer a question if the topic's been clearly decided. The other 360 days of the year I'm more circumspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T04:13:36-07:00","id":234056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or am I just crazy? </div> </div> </div>You played Exalted. Do you remember the bit in Scroll of the Monk about how a mortal martial artist can leap over a boulder, a Terrestrial over a house, a Celestial over a mountain, and a Sidereal can leap through Elsewhere to Heaven?<br /> <br /> Not that you can go to a Godrealm by leaping real good, but that's the sort of escalating benchmarks I'm talking about. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can I also ask that, if you've gt the word count, we get a few examples of really specific purviews? </div> </div> </div>Purviews are still very much in flux, but it's something I'd like to see, certainly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T04:15:05-07:00","id":234057,"title":"","content":"That sounds really really good...<br /> <br /> When I read stuff like that, as well as the Trinity update, as well as all the innovative and awesome stuff Exalted has been hinted as being, I really feel like we're about to enter another golden age of RPGs, spearheaded by White Wolf (ok, Onyx Path, but I'm old and I like to reminisce...).<br /> <br /> Not the same type we had in the late eighties with the Lake Geneva - FASA enthusiastic duality, and certainly not like the D20 boom, more like the true punch in the nose / complete upheaval of players' imaginary landscapes that came from Vampire and cWoD in the late 90's.<br /> We're now getting games that build narrative challenges and quantum physics in their mechanics ! This really feels like our humble hobby is entering a new age of storytelling that blends modern narration with mythology with real world mechanics...<br /> <br /> I like.<br /> <br /> (Also, kudos to you all, artists and craftsmen, who enable and support our addiction to an outlet for our creative frustrations)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1609-fumble","name":"Fumble","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:34:53-07:00","id":234132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=234056#post234056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You played Exalted. Do you remember the bit in Scroll of the Monk about how a mortal martial artist can leap over a boulder, a Terrestrial over a house, a Celestial over a mountain, and a Sidereal can leap through Elsewhere to Heaven?<br /> <br /> Not that you can go to a Godrealm by leaping real good, but that's the sort of escalating benchmarks I'm talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not actually played Exalted, I've decided to get into it with 3rd ed though. I think I understand what you're going for there with the reference though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I assume then that achieveing the tasks of a lower benchmark than your own become pretty trivial? So a God of the Sun, Stars and Celestial bodies with little skill in jumping could still jump over a boulder pretty trivially simply through dint of being a God? Or is that kind of competence more gated behind character options so that not every God can vault a boulder?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T07:37:25-07:00","id":234168,"title":"","content":"I would imagine--and I have no way of knowing for sure--that for the most part that would be the case: Neall seems to describe the lower bounds of a god's power being &quot;merely&quot; a strong and capable mortal.<br /> <br /> I imagine at that point it becomes &quot;what would a strong and capable mortal be capable of in this setting?&quot; But if we're slotting &quot;strong and capable mortal&quot; into the same tier as &quot;mortal martial artist&quot; as Exalted...then I imagine the answer is yes. Unless you're some sort of Hephaestus-type character whose physical incapability is part of their Legend. At that point, I personally imagine you may even become <i>less</i> capable of acts of physical prowess as you gain more from your divine nature.<br /> <br /> Again, just musing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 08-19-2014, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:38:58-07:00","id":234292,"title":"","content":"It all sounds interesting, but very very tricky to pull of mechanically in anything other than clockwork level of complexity or just sweeping rules away for narrative.<br /> <br /> And it mentioned &quot;God Machine update&quot; as an inspiration. (Shudder)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:10:49-07:00","id":234705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=234292#post234292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it mentioned &quot;God Machine update&quot; as an inspiration. (Shudder)</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of how GM handles extended resisted actions, things like down &amp; dirty combat, and narrative modifiers to a dice pool? It's in the DNA. <br /> <br /> I believe my words at the panel were something along the lines of &quot;Exalted and God-Machine both went two separate ways on the Storyteller tree, and our system is from a different root that kind of leans against the tree. &quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:51:35-07:00","id":235581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=233619#post233619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Legend has certain themes according to the dot rating, which may be &quot;mantled&quot; by the god to produce certain divine attributes and power sets. These are acquired by a system of heroic deeds (both in actual play or in an outright character generation). If you're play a Scion, your first dot is always, &quot;Scion of X, God of Y,&quot; which allows you to adopt a lesser set of powers of your parent's most famous mantle. While parentage is clear and may even trace back generations through the Legend system, Scions needn't (and, in fact, it's hard for them) be clones of their parents. Certain relics may be Legend dots, meaning you can't mantle those powers without them.<br /> - <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Zeus, Jupiter and Tinia </span></span>are all the same god, but that god may be mantling different dots of Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I wonder, in this system, if Kali and Parvati will be one deity or two. While Scion 1e's general approach necessitated that they be treated as different Gods, it would actually be more fitting for them to be different mantles of the same deity. To that end, I wonder how different these mantles can be from each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T06:22:13-07:00","id":236410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=233619#post233619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- There are three individual scaling mechanisms - Tiers (and no, I didn't explain what they were), Attributes, <b>(other thing). </b>There's also an environmental scaling mechanism; DaveB likened it to Batman being street-level in his own comics while still fighting cosmic aliens with the Justice League. In some settings, a god may be all-powerful in their Godrealm but &quot;merely&quot; a strong and capable mortal in the place furthest divorced from their themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not very enthused with some of these ideas. It seems to totally throw out the idea that gods from different pantheons could even come into conflict inside their own Godreal from outsiders. Why doesn't this scaling protect them from other supernatural threats like the Aesir from different giants? And it seems to aiming to remove knacks, one of the better parts of the Epic Attribute system (which itself seems like it is mostly removed). :-/<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=233619#post233619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Legend has certain themes according to the dot rating, which may be &quot;mantled&quot; by the god to produce certain divine attributes and power sets. These are acquired by a system of heroic deeds (both in actual play or in an outright character generation). If you're play a Scion, your first dot is always, &quot;Scion of X, God of Y,&quot; which allows you to adopt a lesser set of powers of your parent's most famous mantle. While parentage is clear and may even trace back generations through the Legend system, Scions needn't (and, in fact, it's hard for them) be clones of their parents. Certain relics may be Legend dots, meaning you can't mantle those powers without them.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm pretty happy that clone-itus is going away, I'm wary of Relics being a 'level up' item. Players will do their utmost to abuse that sort of system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T13:54:30-07:00","id":236904,"title":"","content":"I actually don't know how you garnered either of those concerns from what I said, Arthur. <br /> <br /> Epic Attributes, or &quot;so many successes that dice pools are irrelevant&quot; are going away. Attributes that are epic and capable of incredible deeds remain. <br /> <br /> As for the Legend system, what I meant is that &quot;Wielder of Mjolnir&quot; is part of Thor's Legend; the artifact is a meaningful part of him. It's a part of him, and he can evoke special powers that are above and beyond what another god holding the same weapon (say, Beta Ray Bill) could. Not to say that it's not an incredible artifact in it's own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T11:12:55-07:00","id":237147,"title":"","content":"While I agree that the epic progression system is a little overbalanced, I don't think an absolute removal is the way to go. Auto-success adders are a pretty integral part of feeling super.<br /> <br /> It would be like removing autos from potence.<br /> <br /> Now that the invested legend (ie. Mythic ownership) makes a lot better sense than some of your legend (points) are tied to your relic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","user":"ArthurHansen","date":". 08-23-2014, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T11:31:45-07:00","id":237175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=237147#post237147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that the epic progression system is a little overbalanced, I don't think an absolute removal is the way to go. Auto-success adders are a pretty integral part of feeling super.<br /> <br /> or would be like removing autos from potence.<br /> <br /> Now that the invested legend (ie. Mythic ownership) makes a lot better sense than some of your legend (points) are tied to your relic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it really the auto-successes that matter or that they let you perform basic actions effortlessly and then pull off crazy superhuman feats?<br /> <br /> If you could hold the heaven's across your shoulders with 3 successes would that feel less super than holding the heavens across your shoulders with 23 successes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T13:10:47-07:00","id":237268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=236904#post236904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Epic Attributes, or &quot;so many successes that dice pools are irrelevant&quot; are going away. Attributes that are epic and capable of incredible deeds remain.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like great news.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Legend system, what I meant is that &quot;Wielder of Mjolnir&quot; is part of Thor's Legend; the artifact is a meaningful part of him. It's a part of him, and <b>he can evoke special powers that are above and beyond what another god holding the same weapon (say, Beta Ray Bill) could. </b>Not to say that it's not an incredible artifact in it's own right.</div> </div> </div> </div> (emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> And that sounds super awesome. I'm really looking forward to Scion 2e. Please hurry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T16:11:16-07:00","id":237482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=237175#post237175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you could hold the heaven's across your shoulders with 3 successes would that feel less super than holding the heavens across your shoulders with 23 successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Also, holding the heavens across your shoulders is at LEAST a 60+ success feat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T16:42:07-07:00","id":237503,"title":"","content":"Oh, thank god - all those superfluous successes and dice really killed the game for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T03:55:43-07:00","id":238082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=237503#post237503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, thank god - all those superfluous successes and dice really killed the game for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am completely the other way around. The extra successes really divided up the 'tiers of the game. Heros did hero stuff, demigods had their range, and Gods were left to the cosmic changes worthy of their time. Unless they really have a strong mechanic to showcase the Divine kicking ass, I'm very disappointed.<br /> <br /> Then again, everything coming out of the GenCon panel is disappointing. I'm not looking forward to the smushing together of Gods at all. Or what seems to be a loss of purviews.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T07:02:40-07:00","id":238164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=238082#post238082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, everything coming out of the GenCon panel is disappointing. I'm not looking forward to the smushing together of Gods at all. <b>Or what seems to be a loss of purviews. </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Curious about this. Would you explain?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T07:11:16-07:00","id":238168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=237175#post237175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it really the auto-successes that matter or that they let you perform basic actions effortlessly and then pull off crazy superhuman feats?<br /> <br /> If you could hold the heaven's across your shoulders with 3 successes would that feel less super than holding the heavens across your shoulders with 23 successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's counter-thematic to the entire d10 success system, so yes.<br /> <br /> I think that's why the Spirit 'succeed perfectly' system in Exalted annoys me so terribly, because it doesn't actually mechanically show that they are perfect in skill, it just happens because.<br /> <br /> Hercules was the strongest because of his strength, not because he happened to choose a knack 'can pick anything up' and actually only has a Strength 5 Athletics 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","user":"ArthurHansen","date":". 08-23-2014, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T07:21:20-07:00","id":238174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=238164#post238164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Curious about this. Would you explain?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And here I am looking at the Purviews for Scion 2E.<br /> <br /> (Seriously. <i>What?</i> who told you that?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T08:20:34-07:00","id":238202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArturHansen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that the epic progression system is a little overbalanced, I don't think an absolute removal is the way to go. Auto-success adders are a pretty integral part of feeling super.<br /> <br /> It would be like removing autos from potence.</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 <i>does</i> remove autos from Potence unless you spend a blood point, but I'm not going to quibble. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There isn't zero room for autosuccess adders - I actually vastly prefer them to diceadders. But the stat giving you an automatic 60+ autosuccesses? The game breaks down and dice rolls become utterly irrelevant. It's a diceless comparative action at that point, and we have more elegant ways to narratively describe diceless actions that succeed due to the might of those involved. This is the same company that did Imperial Mysteries, and I'm the guy who edited Nobilis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=238082#post238082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am completely the other way around. The extra successes really divided up the 'tiers of the game. Heros did hero stuff, demigods had their range, and Gods were left to the cosmic changes worthy of their time. Unless they really have a strong mechanic to showcase the Divine kicking ass, I'm very disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest problem with Epic Attributes was their sense of scale, to be frank. At higher levels, a single dot completely obviated the need for a die roll against someone even slightly lesser. If Hermes has Epic Dexterity 10 and Hermod has Epic Dexterity 8, it's not even a close race, it's the former god totally outclassing the latter despite a very similar arena and purview.<br /> <br /> (It's an example. We're not bringing Sleipnir into play, though I'd argue the horse is a discernable part of Hermod's Legend.)<br /> <br /> Gods in a different tier treat their actions <i>far</i> differently from demigods and heroes in other tiers. There are multiple systems of scale at work here; our goal is play ability and ease of use at the table, and not requiring six massive die rolls to perform one mighty feat. That said, if you wanted to math out the benchmarks, I doubt you'd be disappointed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then again, everything coming out of the GenCon panel is disappointing. I'm not looking forward to the smushing together of Gods at all. Or what seems to be a loss of purviews. </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry that the Gen Con panel disappoints you, and I'm absolutely willing to discuss things with a longtime fan. Preserving and expanding the same feel as classic Scion - development of heroes through an epic story that showcases their development from heroes to gods, while keeping an emphasis on high drama and action - is a major concern of the writers.<br /> <br /> If your chief disappointments are what you've stated, though, I'm at something of a loss.<br /> <br /> What I said was that Tinia, Zeus and Jupiter are three aspects of the same god from a different lens of people and worship within the same regions. I <i>didn't</i> say that Perun, Indra and Zeus are the same god (they're demonstrably not, though leader archetypes do tend to have a strong sky element to them). Cocidus isn't Mars, but he might also belong to the Gaulish Celts while the latter god remains decidedly with the Greco-Roman gods. Guanyin is likely the same aspect, but possessing membership in <i>three</i> pantheons. Why not? Who doesn't like the goddess of compassion?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure the first edition mentions Tinia at all, but we are going for accuracy and a sense of verisimilitude, and a way for heroes, demigods and gods to embody different aspects and mythological concepts without compromising play.<br /> <br /> And, uh, we <i>do</i> have Purviews. In fact, they're being greatly expanded and focused. The old division of elemental power (Purviews) and divine tricks and charms (Knacks) is still very much part of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-23-2014, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T09:04:44-07:00","id":238249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=238202#post238202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V20 <i>does</i> remove autos from Potence unless you spend a blood point, but I'm not going to quibble. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There isn't zero room for autosuccess adders - I actually vastly prefer them to diceadders. But the stat giving you an automatic 60+ autosuccesses? The game breaks down and dice rolls become utterly irrelevant. It's a diceless comparative action at that point, and we have more elegant ways to narratively describe diceless actions that succeed due to the might of those involved. This is the same company that did Imperial Mysteries, and I'm the guy who edited Nobilis.,</div> </div> </div> </div>You kind of ignored my comment about scaling, but not removing epic ratings. That sounds like you've already decided on this and we are now being told to 'just like it or else'.<br /> <br /> The last game system that decided to be that drastic in changing mechanics was 4e d&amp;d, which made me drop their system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","user":"ArthurHansen","date":". 08-23-2014, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T09:37:05-07:00","id":238287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That sounds like you've already decided on this and we are now being told to 'just like it or else'. </div> </div> </div>Attributes are a definite scaling mechanism, and like I said I'm not sure how you got the idea that gods can't be threatened within their Godrealms. The environment scaling affects pretty much everybody; that's the definition of &quot;environmental&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's no &quot;or else&quot; in there, or a command to just like it. The system is still in flux, and if you still don't like it when you see it, you can voice that opinion in open development.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Tell you what, though. Since this seems to be a point of contention, I'll do a blog post during open development that does a math comparison between Epics, Megas and what we're doing with the new system. The former two have a lot of issues that we're trying to avoid, even as we're building a system that can handle classifying people with divine or superheroic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-23-2014, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T10:02:20-07:00","id":238295,"title":"","content":"On the scaling attributes, I really don't think tiered stats will give the same feel. While godly dex may say that you can dance on a pinhead, but only had a couple of dice for Dex+brawl so gets beat up by a hero in a silly way.<br /> <br /> or even worse, the hero just can't hit him 'because' he's a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","user":"ArthurHansen","date":". 08-23-2014, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T10:10:47-07:00","id":238303,"title":"","content":"My problem with bringing together Gods from different Pantheons is that it is <i>hugely</i> dependent on the amount of research involved.<br /> <br /> There was recently a very long, rather contentious thread about Native American figures and how anyone doing light research will decide that all the coyote-related figures in North and Central America are the same &quot;Coyote&quot; just wearing different masks. But that isn't true if you dig down and actually research on a per-tribe basis instead of a generic &quot;Native American&quot; level. The combination of non-European figures is a hugely problematic issue because it reinforces the dated, colonialistic ideas that &quot;natives&quot; are just big groups of &quot;others&quot; that don't matter as much or have as much cultural development as Europeans. <br /> <br /> Tinia seems very close to Zeus and Jupiter (who <i>are</i> the same figure), but if you really get into Etruscan mythology there are some figures that don't mesh with their Roman-assigned counterparts. Again, because of the nature of the culture involved, that takes a good bit of research. Most of it isn't available in English, either.<br /> <br /> So I'm very concerned that Scion 2nd Edition be careful of who it decides is just a 'mantle' of someone else. Especially for figures from Africa, Oceania, the Americas and (to a lesser degree) Asia. Asia has some of the most active and powerful polytheistic religions in the world, so those figures are less likely to be lumped together. It's hard to do that when there's billions of people to talk to and easily accessible resources for them. The historical religions of the New World and Africa are not in such a good place, even though there are still active communities that follow some traditions. It's nothing like, say, Hinduism or Shinto or Taoism just by sheer numbers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T12:45:43-07:00","id":238434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=238168#post238168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hercules was the strongest because of his strength, not because he happened to choose a knack 'can pick anything up' and actually only has a Strength 5 Athletics 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something here. It seems related to the post above dealing with Thor and his hammer. Legend needs to be more than a number.<br /> I'm reading posts that want to dismiss religion and their worshippers, but...Thor is pretty much one with Mjolnir. Heracles is all about strength. The legends are tied together with religion (Why else call them gods? Or are we going the comic book route and call them aliens...I mean Supermen?)<br /> However, what if legends are forgotten? I can understand why we'd still refer to them as the gods, after all, there was a time when they had no worshippers and still were the powers they were then.<br /> Sorry, I'm rambling incoherently. I'm just picturing a fight between Thor and Sucellus and seeing a contest that would be decided by...fate? Morality (who was more right than wrong?) Story teller fiat I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=238303#post238303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was recently a very long, rather contentious thread about Native American figures and how anyone doing light research will decide that all the coyote-related figures in North and Central America are the same &quot;Coyote&quot; just wearing different masks. But that isn't true if you dig down and actually research on a per-tribe basis instead of a generic &quot;Native American&quot; level. The combination of non-European figures is a hugely problematic issue because it reinforces the dated, colonialistic ideas that &quot;natives&quot; are just big groups of &quot;others&quot; that don't matter as much or have as much cultural development as Europeans.</div> </div> </div> </div>O sure lets open up old wounds...threads...whatever.<br /> I'll just say that if someone had posted what they dug up on Coyote (specifically him, since he is prevalent all over the southwest) that was oh-so-very different...but no one did. So either they didn't do the homework, or they did, and what they found wasn't really different at all and still think if they just dig a little more... (Of course, the old reliable just &quot;google it,&quot; was entertaining.)<br /> But if you've finally found something that isn't superficial and shows that 'hey, we've a whole pack of coyotes that are individuals in their respective tribes...' Well, I've posted before when I was wrong, and I'll do it again.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T15:45:01-07:00","id":238631,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Given that the folks behind the JSR website are apparently involved in making sure that <b>Scion 2e</b>'s gods and mythologies are authentic, I'm not terribly worried. Will it be flawless? I'll be surprised if it is, as I'm not sure that &quot;perfection&quot; can even be meaningfully <i>defined</i>, let alone achieved. But I'll also be surprised if it isn't an order of magnitude better than <b>Scion 1e</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The fact that Zeus, Jupiter, and Tinia are different mantles of the same god doesn't mean that the Etruscan mythology is being mashed together with the Greek and Roman mythologies; rather, it means that the &quot;fuzzy edges&quot; of the different mythologies is being acknowledged: people of different regions were often influenced by the mythologies of their neighbors.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Trying to get the full post posted. 08-23-2014, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:29:27-07:00","id":238663,"title":"","content":"The folks behind JSR WERE assisting with Scion 2E. They left and are now making their own game.<br /> <br /> Edit: As to the loss of purviews, I must have misread an earlier post that said Purviewxs were basically Professional Training a la GMC; which I interpreted as 'purviews as we know it are gone'. If I am wrong about that, I'll be ecstatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 08-23-2014, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:54:54-07:00","id":238678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=238663#post238663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must have misread an earlier post that said Purviewxs were basically Professional Training a la GMC; which I interpreted as 'purviews as we know it are gone'. If I am wrong about that, I'll be ecstatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Purviews allow access and influence over a particular system topic. Mundane Purviews do resemble an expanded Professional Training a bit, but Supernatural Purviews can be far more.<br /> <br /> So they're, &quot;As you know it,&quot; but plus other stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-23-2014, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:56:37-07:00","id":238679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=238287#post238287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Tell you what, though. Since this seems to be a point of contention, I'll do a blog post during open development that does a math comparison between Epics, Megas and what we're doing with the new system. The former two have a lot of issues that we're trying to avoid, even as we're building a system that can handle classifying people with divine or superheroic powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fairly reasonable and I look forward to it.<br /> <br /> I have some serious reservations on the only difference between hero strength/intelligence and god intelligence is 'just because'.<br /> <br /> It would feel really weird that your 'normal intelligence' turns into 'godly intelligence' at high legend as a god, even if you never put a single dot into it after creation. It removes playing the guy that isn't too smart, or never really notices things. Because they are going to be innately better than a mortal even above being able to roll 10s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T22:40:20-07:00","id":238866,"title":"","content":"It makes sense that you can have a Purview of Law, or a Purview of Athletics or a Purview of Craft just as easily as a Purview of Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T03:34:09-07:00","id":239008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=238663#post238663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The folks behind JSR WERE assisting with Scion 2E. They left and are now making their own game. Edit: As to the loss of purviews, I must have misread an earlier post that said Purviewxs were basically Professional Training a la GMC; which I interpreted as 'purviews as we know it are gone'. If I am wrong about that, I'll be ecstatic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mortal-scale Purviews are things like &quot;Cop&quot; or &quot;ER Doctor&quot;. Divine Purviews are things like &quot;War&quot; or &quot;Fire&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T05:50:14-07:00","id":239052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=239008#post239008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mortal-scale Purviews are things like &quot;Cop&quot; or &quot;ER Doctor&quot;. Divine Purviews are things like &quot;War&quot; or &quot;Fire&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...ok.<br /> Better to analogize &quot;Cop&quot; with &quot;Justice;&quot; &quot;Doctor&quot; with &quot;Health.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T13:48:59-07:00","id":239540,"title":"","content":"In a way, that sounds somewhat like Part Time Gods. Not that that is bad or good, just different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T16:27:59-07:00","id":239662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=239008#post239008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mortal-scale Purviews are things like &quot;Cop&quot; or &quot;ER Doctor&quot;. Divine Purviews are things like &quot;War&quot; or &quot;Fire&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does take a lot of concern away, and it does seem to work towards interesting transitions from mortal Scions into their Godly purposes. That is a lot off of my mind.<br /> <br /> The mantle thing; does that include strange neo-pagan ideas of the Gods? Because I'm looking at a scary scenario of Wiccan worshippers granting the Morrigan a happy maternal not-cpmpletely-insane mantle, which is terrifying to think about ... or is it something that will allow (like Samudra asked) the ability for Kali and Paravati to essentially be the same goddess, just different facets of her?<br /> <br /> And how closely related are gods going to be considered under the mantle requirement to avoid, say, smushing all of the Coyotes into one God, or the closely-connected Thunder Kings of Indo-European mythologies.<br /> <br /> On a tangent, I do apologize for the somewhat doomsday approach from earlier; while I do enjoy nWoD, Scion was the first RPG that I completely fell in love with due to the mythological viewpoint. Shoot, I've even put hundreds of hours 'updating it' with the others in our homebrew project and Change is very scary because while Scion 1E needed a lot of love and duct tape to fix up, it was/is amazing as a setting.<br /> <br /> However, if I'm correct in thinking DaveB's on Scion I'm actually very hopeful because it was the Mage Actual Plays that got me into nWoD in the first place --- and if those themes and ideas that convinced me to become a ST myself are put into Scion 2E, I think I can look at the listed changes without biting off ALL my fingernails. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T19:18:31-07:00","id":239791,"title":"","content":"I have a question!<br /> <br /> Will there be room for a character conversion from 1e to 2e? <br /> <br /> My group has characters with 1k+ experience, having played for years. I have considered using the God Machine system of converting all 5xp to equate to 1 beat, but i don't know if that would work or not.You mentioned it was based of Trinity system, but i don't know anything about that.<br /> <br /> I guess in a nutshell I am asking if we can play our old characters, albeit with a face-lift of sorts; or should they be loving set aside? I don't mind having to start again fresh- but if it is even possible to incorporate the energy of the last edition into the new that would be wonderful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2556-firstaide","name":"Firstaide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T03:24:24-07:00","id":240081,"title":"","content":"So, can mortals gain Purviews like, say, &quot;Wizard/Sorcerer?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T16:23:44-07:00","id":240879,"title":"","content":"I rather like the notion of mantles, covers the topics of purviews/boons, pantheons, and gods with dualistic/multiple natures quite elegantly. Precisely how customizable will new purviews and mantles be?<br /> <br /> That said, put me in the column of preferring the disposal of epic attributes, and attached knacks. Knacks, if anything, if they're to remain at the same power level as Scion 1e should well fall under purviews. The dice pools and numbers of successes were too much to handle, and really disruptive to the game, in Scion 1e...especially when it comes to combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T17:08:47-07:00","id":240905,"title":"","content":"I guess mantles make one more versatile? More powerful?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T02:17:12-07:00","id":241187,"title":"","content":"So when can I throw my money at this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is a signature &lt;-----------","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","name":"Shining Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T09:28:56-07:00","id":241408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shining Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=241187#post241187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when can I throw my money at this?</div> </div> </div> </div>My bank account? I mean, it won't make the game come any faster, and I have nothing to do with Scion, but I wouldn't mind a bit of cash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T09:12:20-07:00","id":242279,"title":"","content":"Neall - Can you estimate when you (or someone, anyone, else of the team) can spill some concrete mechanics? I mean you hinted at the very general function of the system, but i am really curious about it in a much deeper way...i would want to see examples of mechanics at work etc. .<br /> Scion 2 is one of my most anticipated games.<br /> <br /> Thanks for doing this, btw. Answers from the people involved is always a nice thing to have.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/153-ebon-wolf","name":"Ebon Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T21:04:02-07:00","id":243593,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I'm enjoying what I'm hearing so far. I've been doing some in-depth study of Shinto, and I've taken a long, hard look at Vodou, so what's being said for Scion 2E has my interest. I'm curious to see what you'll be doing for scaling. I've idly thought of removing epic attributes from Scion 1E, and doing something like this: Roll Attribute Dice and Skill Dice as separate pools (marked by colour). Human: Attribute Success 1:1, Scion: 2:1, Demigod: 3:1, God: 4:1. So if a god gets 2 successes on his Attribute, they're actually 8 successes. If a demigod gets 2 successes, it's actually 6. The Greek Pantheon do the same thing with Skills. I'm considering it, anyway. It allows for similar dice pools, but with wider effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T02:55:39-07:00","id":243799,"title":"","content":"It's a massively simpler game but OVA has a 'scale' factor. In that if you are superior in the current situation due to your scale you get a flat +5 (which is pretty big but not completely insurmountable).<br /> <br /> E.g.: You are piloting agiant gundam style mecha and get into a pushing match with a super strong superhero. By simple dint of being a giant mecha you get a flat +5, if you've got other strength modifiers those apply too. Conversely if you were trying to evade that giant mecha as the superhero you'd get a +5 to hiding amongst buildings and the winding streets of a city as the scale now favours you.<br /> <br /> I don't imagine that Scion will use as simple a system - but I;ve played games using scaling so know it can work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T17:59:36-07:00","id":247299,"title":"","content":"I was concerned about the Orisha being the representative, though after thinking long about it, I came to some opinions:<br /> <br /> 1. When Scion first started, Shango was called the Loa of Vengence. While it was alright for First Edition, I think that Shango should get a different title to reflect his standing as All-Father to the Orisha while not being alarming to anyone who comes across him. Keeping on using the title Loa of Vengence, makes me think that the African-Americans of Scion are always trying to look for a fight, which shouldn't be the case at all. Other than that, I'm ok with Shango being the leader.<br /> <br /> 2. I have heard that the Yoruba tribe participated in the Black slavery market by giving tribesmen who opposed the chief to White slavers. If there's truth to this, were the Orisha okay with this, and in association, promoting Black slavery? I felt that it would be very paradoxical for a pantheon who represented everyone of African descent.<br /> <br /> 3. I'm still trying to wrap my head on Shango's wife being Erzulie, the Loa of Love. Given the info that you guys gave me, the way of how she treated the other gods, in defense of her husband, makes me think that she created the term, &quot;Mean Girl&quot;. Comparing it to the Olympians, she resembles more like Hera/Juno than Aphrodite/Venus. Does this mean that threats of physical abuse is considered &quot;affection&quot; among the Orisha?<br /> <br /> Please clarify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T18:55:55-07:00","id":247325,"title":"","content":"I'm a little fuzzy in that Greek comparison. I mean wasn't Hera the only one interested in &quot;morality?&quot; To paraphrase a quote; <i>&quot;When mom didn't put up with dad's philandering, they called her a bitch. When she looked the other way they called her a doormat. That stops now. She never cheated on him despite his mistreatment of her. The Queen of Heaven is not to be disrespected.....&quot;</i> Aphrodite seemed more the &quot;mean girl&quot; to me....I'm just wondering...and wandering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T20:47:38-07:00","id":247410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247299#post247299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. When Scion first started, Shango was called the Loa of Vengence. While it was alright for First Edition, I think that Shango should get a different title to reflect his standing as All-Father to the Orisha while not being alarming to anyone who comes across him. Keeping on using the title Loa of Vengence, makes me think that the African-Americans of Scion are always trying to look for a fight, which shouldn't be the case at all. Other than that, I'm ok with Shango being the leader.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shango <i>is</i> the leader of the Orishas. That's the mythology. He's also an Orisha of Vengeance and asswhuppin and generally being an angry, grumpy badass. Scion's writers (hopefully) won't change their portrayal of mythology just to make it more palatable to modern, Western audiences. Furthermore, most Gods are not the &quot;God of Things&quot;. They're divine figures who have a wide portfolio of powers. The concept of each God having a single domain is <i>extremely</i> Greek. It almost never appears anywhere else. Thor isn't the God of Thunder, he's THOR and he happens to do thunder stuff, but also other things. Because of how strongly Greek thought and mythology dominate Western culture, there's a strong desire in pop culture to try forcing other deities into the &quot;God of X&quot; framework that the Greeks had. It doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Let's also be clear, the Orishas are not African-American. They're African. The Yoruba aren't even really &quot;African-American&quot; because they're generally Caribbean, though there are some adherents to their religion who <i>are</i> African-American. Trying to apply modern ethno-nationality to polytheistic historical religions is just silly. Not all African-American Scions will be Orishas. Not all Orishas will be from America. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247299#post247299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I have heard that the Yoruba tribe participated in the Black slavery market by giving tribesmen who opposed the chief to White slavers. If there's truth to this, were the Orisha okay with this, and in association, promoting Black slavery?</div> </div> </div> </div>An immensely complex question, and surely each and every Orisha had different feelings on the issue. However, their feelings are <i>not</i> going to be the feelings of modern, Western Americans. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247299#post247299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt that it would be very paradoxical for a pantheon who represented everyone of African descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to stop right here and address this by itself. <b><i><u>THE ORISHA DO NOT REPRESENT EVERYONE OF AFRICAN DESCENT</u></i></b><u>.</u> They don't represent the Egyptians, the Massai, the Zulu, the Twareg or <i>anyone </i>but the Yoruba. They are not the &quot;Gods of Africa&quot;, they are the Gods of the Yoruba. It would be silly to say they possibly <i>could</i> represent all Africans, just as it would be silly to say the Greeks represent all Europeans or the Japanese represent all of Asia. No culture's Pantheon represents anything <i>but that culture</i>. And, indeed, some cultures have had <i>multiple</i> pantheons at various points in history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247299#post247299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I'm still trying to wrap my head on Shango's wife being Erzulie, the Loa of Love. Given the info that you guys gave me, the way of how she treated the other gods, in defense of her husband, makes me think that she created the term, &quot;Mean Girl&quot;. Comparing it to the Olympians, she resembles more like Hera/Juno than Aphrodite/Venus. Does this mean that threats of physical abuse is considered &quot;affection&quot; among the Orisha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods are generally not held to the same standards of behavior that mortals are, and further more, definitely not to the same standards as modern people, absolutely not to the same standards as <i>Western, </i>modern people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T20:58:16-07:00","id":247414,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Telgar. You said that much more eloquently than I could have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T00:25:32-07:00","id":247559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247410#post247410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thor isn't the God of Thunder, he's THOR and he happens to do thunder stuff, but also other things. Because of how strongly Greek thought and mythology dominate Western culture, there's a strong desire in pop culture to try forcing other deities into the &quot;God of X&quot; framework that the Greeks had. It doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Very, seriously, this. It's an issue I've come across when I've seen some Scion players fretting over what their character is going to become the 'god of', or 'I want to be a &lt;insert&gt; god but &lt;name&gt; has that covered in my pantheon so I can't.'. Sure, the Greeks/Romans were very compartmentalised and you need to have a specific portfolio, but most pantheons seem to be arranged around gods who are known for taking <i>care</i> of something but not necessarily the god <i>of</i> that thing.<br /> <br /> I kind of think the signature character templates did a bit to push the notion of 'God of &lt;thing&gt;'. I could easily have seen Eric proudly telling everyone 'Well if my dad is God of Thunder I'm gonna be the God of Lightning. We're a team!' and I could see Marie Glapion telling her fellow Loa that she wanted to be there for her people who have reason to regret as she does, but I doubt most of the others formally took on any specific portfolio duties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T01:58:43-07:00","id":247643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247559#post247559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. Very, seriously, this. It's an issue I've come across when I've seen some Scion players fretting over what their character is going to become the 'god of', or 'I want to be a &lt;insert&gt; god but &lt;name&gt; has that covered in my pantheon so I can't.'. Sure, the Greeks/Romans were very compartmentalised and you need to have a specific portfolio, but most pantheons seem to be arranged around gods who are known for taking <i>care</i> of something but not necessarily the god <i>of</i> that thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at the sheer number of epithets, functions and portfolios each of the Greek/Roman gods accumulated, while they might be best known as 'God of X', they were considered to take care of a lot more besides. I'd aim the criticism more at later Western civilisation's interpretation of them, which effectively flanderised them, took what they were best known for and made it so it was _all_ they were.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T06:56:06-07:00","id":247806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247410#post247410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shango <i>is</i> the leader of the Orishas. That's the mythology. He's also an Orisha of Vengeance and asswhuppin and generally being an angry, grumpy badass. Scion's writers (hopefully) won't change their portrayal of mythology just to make it more palatable to modern, Western audiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you just did that in your next sentence.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247410#post247410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, most Gods are not the &quot;God of Things&quot;. They're divine figures who have a wide portfolio of powers. The concept of each God having a single domain is <i>extremely</i> Greek. It almost never appears anywhere else. Thor isn't the God of Thunder, he's THOR and he happens to do thunder stuff, but also other things. Because of how strongly Greek thought and mythology dominate Western culture, there's a strong desire in pop culture to try forcing other deities into the &quot;God of X&quot; framework that the Greeks had. It doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a back handed argument against &quot;Greek interpretation&quot; I take it?<br /> Tacitus describes Odin as Mercury, Thor became Jupiter. Of course, Germanica may have seen things a bit different. But one would have to be immersed in that culture to know that. <br /> But Thor isn't the God of Thunder? Really? (Considering Asatru is a recognized religious belief in several countries I'm sure this is just crazy talk.) His very name derives from the word meaning &quot;thunder.&quot; If one wants to change this cultural reality, then they'd have to change his name. That Thor eventually assumed other roles doesn't change what he is; The God of the Storm.<br /> This was a mythological argument you claim? And it reminds me of an atheist telling Catholics that Jesus isn't part of the Trinity because he read up all about it and he sees the Trinity as something different.<br /> Either he's the God of Thunder to ancient Germanica or he's something else to a modern audience. Y'know, to make the idea more &quot;palatable.&quot;<br /> <br /> But since we're speaking of a game...play on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T07:16:46-07:00","id":247821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247806#post247806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Thor isn't the God of Thunder? Really? (Considering Asatru is a recognized religious belief in several countries I'm sure this is just crazy talk.) His very name derives from the word meaning &quot;thunder.&quot; If one wants to change this cultural reality, then they'd have to change his name. That Thor eventually assumed other roles doesn't change what he is; The God of the Storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thor <i>is</i> the Norse God of Thunder, but that's not <i>all</i> he is. He was (and is) heavily invoked for protection, which has nothing directly to do with thunder. He's known for being the God of Thunder, and that's his jam, but he's also a lot of other things. He's been affiliated with all kinds of other acts, beyond storming. It's just that with his fierce temper and desire to protect his family they're the things he's best known for. They're simply not all he is. In much the same way, Ullr is best known for being the winter ski god and hunter, also consecrated oaths and promises.<br /> <br /> There are Aesir gods that you go to for various things because they're the best at them, and in some cases there are no others who actually do that thing (other sky gods are a bit light on among the Aesir) so that tends to become 'their thing' but there's no specific lock on it. Another god coming up among many pantheons, the Aesir in this example, could mainline Sky and not have a bunch of angry Aesir surround them and demand that they not do it because &quot;we already have a thunder god.&quot;. Thor will always be considered the go-to guy for thundering. Newer weather deities will probably find themselves asked to apply themselves in other ways, or at least the others will sit back and watch the friendly competition between two thunder waving ass kickers.<br /> <br /> And, considering Thor's temper, 'thunder' could as easily be a sobriquet gained from his temper as his power to wreak havoc with the weather.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T09:22:52-07:00","id":247910,"title":"","content":"The point I'm making here is that to the Norse, thunder = Thor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T09:38:48-07:00","id":247934,"title":"","content":"Long time lurker, first time poster... Normally, I'm content to just read the the writing on the wall, but this is a topic I felt I had to speak up about...<br /> <br /> So first, hi everyone, nice to meet you! I am so freaking excited about Scion 2nd edition that I can barely wait to spend all my slush fund on it.<br /> <br /> Second, it was always my understanding that Obatala was the leader of the Orisha. He was the first Orisha created by Olodumare. He is the most powerful Orisha, the Lord of the Head, the King of Purity. He is recognised as the head of the Orishas, and he fathered many of the ones to come. He is also the father of humanity.<br /> <br /> Shango, in some traditions, was the name of the third king of the city of Oyo and the fourth king of the Yoruba. He is the Orisha of thunder, power, raw masculinity and a terrible, terrible womaniser. He is not married to Erzulie (Erzulie comes from Haitian traditions, not Yoruba), but he is married to Oba, the Orisha of neglected wives. Shango has taken Oya and Oshun as his concubines and loves them far more than he loves his wife.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where all of this talk is coming from that Shango is the head of the pantheon, but anyway. All that I described up there I learned from Santeria.<br /> <br /> Erzulie is ... not just Erzulie. There are two different ways to interpret Erzulie, though. Some people say there are many Erzulies - the most famous being Erzulie Freda and Erzulie Dantor. They are like sisters who cannot stand the sight of each other, but important to note is that Erzulie Freda is married to Damballah, to Agwe, and to Ogoun. Erzulie Dantor is married to Ti Jean Petro (or is his mother or is his lover, depending on who you ask). Others say that Erzulie Freda and Erzulie Dantor are two aspects of the same loa. One is definitely Rada (Freda), and the other is Petro (Dantor).<br /> <br /> First Edition drove me absolutely crazy with how badly it treated the loa. Needless to say, I pretty much rewrote that whole pantheon for the games I ran.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2789-laume78","name":"laume78","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T09:48:13-07:00","id":247946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>laume78</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247934#post247934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure where all of this talk is coming from that Shango is the head of the pantheon, but anyway. All that I described up there I learned from Santeria.<br /> Thanks for reading!</div> </div> </div> </div>First off thanks for your contribution. The more the merrier I always say.<br /> If I may ask...is your interest in Santeria personal?<br /> Just curious.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T10:38:38-07:00","id":247991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247946#post247946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off thanks for your contribution. The more the merrier I always say.<br /> If I may ask...is your interest in Santeria personal?<br /> Just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome! I'd have rambled a lot more, but I figured I should probably stop before I got bricked. I love talking about this stuff.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how to answer that question though. Yes and no. Yes, in that New Orleans Voodoo, Haitian Vodou, African Vodun, Santeria and all of the other Yoruboid religions are fascinating to the point of obsession for me, and I've been reading every website and book I can get my hands on for the past five years. I grew up hardcore, old-school Roman Catholic, and I had shrines to the saints that I lovingly built and maintained in my room. When I came upon voodoo, years later, it harkened back to the time of my childhood where religion was still something I fervently, lovingly believed in. Yes, the loa of Haiti and the orisha of Santeria used the images of saints to mask their true identities, so it's not quite the same, but in the traditions of the people, I found something I could very deeply relate to. For me, as a child, God was a more distant entity. He was often quite frightening too, given all the talk about Hell flying about. So as a kid, I clung more to the saints and to the Virgin Mary, revering them as friends and family who could 'get me in good with God.'<br /> <br /> And a lot of that is echoed in voodoo (or vodou, vodun, however you want to spell it - I vary the spelling depending on which location I'm referring to).<br /> <br /> The loa and the orishas are intermediaries between humanity and Bondye / Olodumare-Olorun-Olofi. The supreme being, the Creator god, is distant from all of humanity and earth, but the Creator has given power to the orishas and loa to help out humanity. So while vodouisants do not worship the loa and orishas as gods, they are certainly given their due and reverence. They are honoured with shrines, sacrifices, dances, and songs. But they are seen as family and as friends.<br /> <br /> So yes, yes, it is pretty personal to me in that I want to see each loa and orisha given proper, due respect.<br /> <br /> But also no. I'm not an active practicioner. I consider myself a student at best. I left behind actively practicing religion in my teenage years, and so I can't speak with any authority or experience from visiting temples here (I'd have gone to a temple, but there are none near where I live, curse my location!). I can't speak for any mambos or houngans, and I can't speak as someone who knows more than a beginning initiate. Do I believe that the loa / orisha actually exist? Jury's still out on that one, but I believe it's possible that they could. I don't believe anyone has the answers, least of all me.<br /> <br /> I should probably stop rambling again here. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2789-laume78","name":"laume78","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T15:24:18-07:00","id":248167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247410#post247410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shango <i>is</i> the leader of the Orishas. That's the mythology. He's also an Orisha of Vengeance and asswhuppin and generally being an angry, grumpy badass. Scion's writers (hopefully) won't change their portrayal of mythology just to make it more palatable to modern, Western audiences. Furthermore, most Gods are not the &quot;God of Things&quot;. They're divine figures who have a wide portfolio of powers. The concept of each God having a single domain is <i>extremely</i> Greek. It almost never appears anywhere else. Thor isn't the God of Thunder, he's THOR and he happens to do thunder stuff, but also other things. Because of how strongly Greek thought and mythology dominate Western culture, there's a strong desire in pop culture to try forcing other deities into the &quot;God of X&quot; framework that the Greeks had. It doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Let's also be clear, the Orishas are not African-American. They're African. The Yoruba aren't even really &quot;African-American&quot; because they're generally Caribbean, though there are some adherents to their religion who <i>are</i> African-American. Trying to apply modern ethno-nationality to polytheistic historical religions is just silly. Not all African-American Scions will be Orishas. Not all Orishas will be from America.<br /> <br /> First off, congratulations on making me disturbed of all Black people that will be represented in Scion. It makes me worried that every five seconds someone's going to call my character a &quot;cracker&quot; and try to kill him in Shango's name. Second, stop calling me retarded everytime you talk about my culture. Sure, in a social sense, White culture is the autistic kid on the playground (no offense to the viewers), but knocking our copy of Remedial Mythology out of our hands isn't going to make us understand what you're saying. Third, you may say that gods with a single domain may be Greek, but I think that the Greeks learned from Africans. When I saw the list of Loa from the Orisha, there was Agwe, Loa of Water, and there was a Loa of Earth as well. The only three that didn't follow the claim, as far as I could tell from the list, was Shango, his wife, and Eshu.<br /> <br /> Also, contrary to what you say, people actually believe the Yoruba to be strictly African in nature, since the culture came from African slaves.<br /> <br /> <br /> An immensely complex question, and surely each and every Orisha had different feelings on the issue. However, their feelings are <i>not</i> going to be the feelings of modern, Western Americans.<br /> <br /> Again, you're calling my culture retarded. Please stop it.<br /> <br /> I want to stop right here and address this by itself. <b><i><u>THE ORISHA DO NOT REPRESENT EVERYONE OF AFRICAN DESCENT</u></i></b><u>.</u> They don't represent the Egyptians, the Massai, the Zulu, the Twareg or <i>anyone </i>but the Yoruba. They are not the &quot;Gods of Africa&quot;, they are the Gods of the Yoruba. It would be silly to say they possibly <i>could</i> represent all Africans, just as it would be silly to say the Greeks represent all Europeans or the Japanese represent all of Asia. No culture's Pantheon represents anything <i>but that culture</i>. And, indeed, some cultures have had <i>multiple</i> pantheons at various points in history.<br /> <br /> Technically, the Egyptians aren't African, even though their land is in the Sahara Otherwise, we would be calling Egyptians Saharan-Africans. When people say &quot;of African descent&quot; they mean sub-Saharan. Also, the reason why the Orisha represents all Africans is because the book Scion:Origins will have them as the sole representatives of said continent, given that their culture is most prominent in Black culture. Let the books ease us in to the other tribes. No need to rush. Also, technically, the Olympians did represent all of Western Europe, thanks to the Roman Empire, and then when that fell, the Aesir was the representative of Europe above the Mediterranean, before Christianity booted it out. And sure, China had it's shen, but it didn't stop the Kami from trying. That thing about multiple pantheons I would have to take a while to take it iin.<br /> <br /> <br /> Gods are generally not held to the same standards of behavior that mortals are, and further more, definitely not to the same standards as modern people, absolutely not to the same standards as <i>Western, </i>modern people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again please stop calling my culture <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">stupid. Mod edit, Darksider.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 09-03-2014, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T17:44:36-07:00","id":248309,"title":"","content":"I'm calling Western culture stupid by pointing out that it has significant differences from historical cultures from different continents? Jackalope, I really don't understand where that's coming from. Western culture is fine. It's great, even. It's got problems, but so does every culture. That does not mean I should stop pointing out where it needs to improve, or where the differences it has from other cultures need to be considered.<br /> <br /> To be honest, Jackalope, I really had trouble following your post at all. I am not saying that all Black people (another construct of modern, Western culture, because Africa isn't a culture, it's a continent) will be angry, racist and violent. Holy crap, how did that come out of what I said? I said that Shango is the leader of the Yoruba Pantheon and that he is a violent, angry figure. That says <i>nothing</i> about the actions and attitudes of any member of that culture, <i>much less</i> any other culture. I never mentioned racial slurs at all. I am <i>terribly</i> confused by your response to what I said. <br /> <br /> Where are you getting that Agwe is the Loa of Water and these other things? They're far more than that. Far, far more complicated and detailed. They exist widely beyond the narrow idea that they're the &quot;God of X&quot;, which is what I was trying to explain. It tends to be a very, very Greek (and thus Western) idea that Gods are narrowly defined. That has a lot to do with the Greek, and later Roman, and now Western, cultures being obsessed with strict categorization and labels. The Greeks specifically had a God of <i>everything</i> and generally of only one, maybe two or three things. That is not a viewpoint shared by many other cultures. So, while yes, Agwe is associated with water, he's many other things. It's not a simple 1:1 correlation, and it's important to know that.<br /> <br /> <br /> I did not say that no one believes the Yoruba are African. It's come up in the past, and will again in the future, that people are uncertain about where the Yoruba are from, what their mythology is and what its connection to Voodoo and the Loa is. It's a complex issue and needs to be addressed correctly. There's lots of room for confusion, because it isn't an area that gets a lot of attention in Western pop culture.<br /> <br /> <br /> Egypt is in Africa. Egyptians are Africans. Physically, they're more similar to Middle Easterners, as are many inhabitants of Northern Africa, but there are a number of cultural similarities with the rest of Africa. &quot;Africa&quot; means Africa. If you want to just talk about sub-Saharan Africa (still a HUGE region with hundreds of cultures and languages) then that's different. I admit that &quot;most people&quot; don't tend to think of Egypt as part of Africa, they often lump it in with the Middle East, which it <i>also</i> shares a great deal of culture and language with. Just because Egypt doesn't fit with the pop-culture view of Africa doesn't mean it isn't there, and shouldn't be considered. It was a huge influence on its neighbors all along the northern and eastern coasts. <br /> <br /> <br /> Just because there's only one culture from a given continent in Scion books <i><b><u>does not mean that culture represents all cultures of that continent</u></b></i>. It only means that that culture is the only one from a given continent. The Yoruba no more represent the Zulu than the Greeks represent the Irish. The Chinese do not represent Korea. The Aztecs do not represent the Cherokee. Scion is not organized by continents, it's organized by cultures, and those that were picked to be in the corebook are simply the ones most familiar to Western audiences (the game's main target demographic). The Norse represent <i>only the Nordic People</i>. They don't represent the Sami, or the Baltics, or the Slavs. They don't even represent the French, Spanish, Portuguese, Welsh or Scottish. It could be argued they represent the English, but that's dicey. <br /> <br /> <br /> No one, especially not me, is saying that Western culture is stupid, or that people with a limited understanding of world mythology (a Remedial Book as you mention) are stupid. They're just not educated. Scion can be educated, and can educate. It should do those things, <i>especially</i> the first. It <i>needs</i> to be educated. It needs to be informed. The writers need to do research, and they need to provide a fair and respectful perspective about the cultures they're dealing with instead of reducing them to stereotypes as has been done so often in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":". 09-03-2014, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T19:21:13-07:00","id":248381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>laume78</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=247991#post247991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome! I'd have rambled a lot more, but I figured I should probably stop before I got bricked. I love talking about this stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>ooo...I'm all about rambling, so I'm right there with you.<br /> <br /> Thank you for sharing though.<br /> <br /> I've read a lot on what some refer to as &quot;pagan&quot; beliefs. My own personal obsessions tend to lean towards druids and what is referred to today as &quot;Wicca.&quot; With druids there really isn't much to go on, and it's that mystery that keeps me fascinated. (oh, I'm sure someone will say they have it figured out. Just blowing in the wind to me) The same goes for wicca...but just the opposite. There's so much to go on one doesn't know where to start sometimes.<br /> They were and still are magic worker, priest/priestess, herbalist, pagan and heretic and every shade in between. (Despite the fact that the term carries a lot of baggage, I personally prefer the term &quot;witch&quot; over &quot;Wiccan.&quot;)<br /> <br /> And then there are many deities that were believed to have been associated with witchcraft. (except Hecate and Baba Yaga. Neither were merely &quot;associated,&quot; but were at times typified as witches.)<br /> We have some celtic witches...fairy witches...night witches...white witches. (although I personally dislike &quot;coloring&quot;), Dianic witches...That's the good and bad thing about being a witch. Beliefs can vary from one to another and all still can be a witch. Acceptance and tolerance are two key words when it comes being a wiccan/witch. However, because of this lack of a consistent doctrine, it sometimes becomes frustrating to get solid info on what &quot;real&quot; witches are. (Such has evolved over years...to what we have today.)<br /> <br /> I find Wiccan beliefs, in all its frustrating variety to be reassuring in a way that still puzzles me.<br /> <br /> Some stuff I posted elsewhere...I'm not sure all the links work;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The following is from the 1692 testimony of Robert Downer in Cotton Mather's <a href=\"http://etext.lib.virginia.edu/salem/witchcraft/speccol/cmather/table/\" target=\"_blank\">Wonders of the Invisible World</a>:<br /> <br /> <i>That this Prisoner being some Years ago prosecuted at Court for a Witch, he then said unto her, He believed she was a Witch. Whereat she being dissatisfied, said, That some She-Devil would shortly fetch him away! Which words were heard by others, aw well as himself. The Night following, as he lay in his Bed, there came in at the Window, the likeness of a Cat, which flew upon him, took fast hold of his Throat, lay on him a considerable while, and almost killed him. At length he remembered what Susanna Martin had threat'ned the Day before; and with much striving he cried out, Avoid, thou She-Devil! In the Name of God the Father, the Son, and the Holy Ghost, Avoid! Whereupon it left him, leap'd on the Floor, and flew out at the Window. And there also came in several testimoines, that before ever Downer spoke a word of this Accident, Susanna Marin and her Family had related, How this Downer had been handled!</i><br /> <br /> (Yes there\u2019s plenty in that link, which makes one wonder about Cotton Mather.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.shanmonster.com/witch/witches/agnes.html\" target=\"_blank\">Agnes</a> wife of Ode, freed (1209) after passing the red-hot-iron test for witchcraft. She carried a red-hot bar of iron and was not seared\u2026<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.shanmonster.com/witch/witches/cleary.html\" target=\"_blank\">Bridget Cleary</a> In 1894 in Clonmel, County Tipperary in Ireland, Bridget Cleary, the Faerie Witch of Clonmel, was burned to death\u2026<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.shanmonster.com/witch/witches/faerie.html\" target=\"_blank\">The Faery Witch</a> In the 1600s in the North of England, a man was brought into court on charges of witchcraft. He claimed to use a powder to heal sicknesses, and offered to lead the judge to the faerie hill where he obtained the medicine. Although the judge was harsh, the jury refused to convict him\u2026<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.shanmonster.com/witch/witches/gowdie.html\" target=\"_blank\">Isobel Gowdie</a>, , the renowned &quot;Queen of Scottish Witches&quot; confessed in 1662 she had frequent dealings with faeries. Gowdie claimed to have often journeyed to Faerieland, entering through various mounds and caverns...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.shanmonster.com/witch/witches/pearson.html\" target=\"_blank\">Alison Pearson</a> In 1588, Alison Pearson of Byrehill was accused of invoking demonic spirits. She was also accused of having a faerie familiar\u2026<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.shanmonster.com/witch/witches/zlito.html\" target=\"_blank\">Zlito</a> &quot;Sorcerer of 14th century. Attached to court of King Wenceslaus of Bohemia. Reputed to have had skill in levitation.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, here\u2019s a more objective look on the case of <a href=\"http://www.rootsweb.com/%7Enwa/sm.html\" target=\"_blank\">Susanna Martin</a><br /> Which of course begs the question; &quot;Was there any truth to the accusations?<br /> The many tales of witches using magic\u2026were they all just tales?<br /> <br /> William of Malmesbury tells the story of the &quot;witch of Berkeley&quot; (1142):<br /> <i>&quot;About that time a certaine woman in Berkeley accustomed to evil arts, when as upon a certaine day shee kept a feast, a Chough which shee used delicately to feede cackled more loud and distinctly than shee was wont to doe, which when shee heard, the knife fell out of her hand, her countenance waxed pale, and havinge fetched a deepe groane, with a sigh said, 'nowe this day is the plowe come to my last furrowe;' which beinge said, a messenger cominge in, declared to her the death of her Sonne, and of all her Family exposed to present ruine; The woman presently laye downe and called to her such of her other children as were Monkes and a Nunne, who cominge shee thus spake unto them; 'I a wicked follower of an evil art and worse life vainly thought to have beene defended by your praiers, nowe I desire to be eased by you of my torments, because judgement is given against my soul, but peradventure you may keepe my body if it bee fast sewed in a stag's skin; make yee for mee a chest of stone, fast bound and cemented with iron and lead, settinge the same upright, and also bound about with three iron chaines; use singers of Psalmes for forty nights, and pay for soe many Masses by daies; and if I shall soe lie for three nights, on the fourth day bury my body in the ground; But all was in vaine, for in the two first nights which the psalmes were in soundinge, the Divells havinge easily broken the doores, as lightly brake the two utmost iron chaines; and on the third night about cock-crowinge, the place shakinge, one with a terrible countenance and of a mighty tall stature, havinge broken open the cover of the chest commanded the dead body to arise, who answeringe that shee could not by reason of the bonds; bee thou loosed quoth hee, but to thy woe; and presently all the barres being broken, hee draweth her out of the Church, and setteth her upon a blacke horse, neighinge before the doore, aud soe went away with loud soundinge cries heard four miles of.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> (This was also told in the<br /> <a href=\"http://www.rotwang.co.uk/hob_chapter_01.html\" target=\"_blank\">Polichronicon of Reinulph of Chester</a>, sometimes referred to as the Polychronicon of Ranulph Higden.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.shanmonster.com/witch/hunters/tilbury.html\" target=\"_blank\">Gervaise of Tilbury</a>:<br /> Writing about 1214, Gervaise of Tilbury tells stories that he claims to have garnered from eye-witnesses. Men and women ride out at night over long distances. Certain people have seen their flight as they passed over land and sea. They are able to fly all over the globe, so long as none of them makes the mistake of uttering the name of Christ while in flight, for this will make them immediately fall and plunge to the ground. At Arles, Gervaise himself saw a woman who had thus been plunged into the Rhone and soaked as far as her navel. The witches enter people's houses in the course of these nocturnal journeys. They disturb sleepers by sitting on their chests and causing nightmares of suffocation and falling. They have sexual relations with sleeping men. They suck blood, steal infants from their beds, and rummage through baskets and bins for food. They take the form of cats, wolves, or other animals at will\u2026<br /> <br /> After the 17th century intellectualism began replacing many ideas about religion. (Some Christians in Europe were more stubborn)<br /> <br /> Rationalist denied that witches existed at all. (Interesting work from 1869, <a href=\"http://www.hti.umich.edu/cgi/t/text/text-idx?c=moa;idno=ACA6563\" target=\"_blank\">Annals of Witchcraft in New England</a> by Samuel G. Drake Witchcraft; beliefs were superstitions, revivals of demonic belief and wholly artificial. Sir Francis Dashwood presided over the Hellfire Club (AKA &quot;The Friars of St Francis of Wycombe&quot;, &quot;The Monks of Medmenham&quot;, or &quot;The Order of Knights of West Wycombe, which seemed to be nothing more than an exercise in debauchery.<br /> <br /> Interest in the occult grew in the late 19th century and into the early 20th century. We see Aleister Crowley, A.E. Waite, Macgregor Mathers among others calling themselves practitioners of witchcraft. (I honestly don\u2019t see it in these personages.)<br /> <br /> Perhaps we see witchcraft in its evolution. From it\u2019s earliest beginnings with Medea worshipping Hecate, (according to the literature.) to recent times and <a href=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/southampton/features/newforest/witches.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">Sybil Leek</a> for example.<br /> <br /> Magic and religion entwined\u2026<br /> <br /> Margaret Murray\u2019s thesis may have been fallacy ridden, but she had in mind a coherent religion that survived. Ironic that witchcraft survived\u2026just not &quot;coherently.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.spellsnow.com/images/witchcraft_book.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  Looks like shanmonster pulled her website. So bye-bye links...*sniffs* 09-03-2014, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T11:52:58-07:00","id":249026,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the links on Wicca! I'll be reading those forthwith. ^_^<br /> <br /> Heh. Inconsistency is a part of voodoo/vodou/vodun as well. Finding a definitive source is impossible. Traditions and beliefs can differ from houngan to houngan, from sosyete to sosyete. What's practiced by one peristyle may be different from another just down the road (for example, the aforementioned, differing views on Erzulie Freda and Erzulie Dantor).<br /> <br /> In a lot of ways, I don't envy the Scion 2e writers their task, but I'm eager to see what they've done. How do you put together a pantheon like this that has so much conflicting information? Subsets and mantlings do strike me as pretty darn clever, though I imagine no matter what they do, people will House Rule changes to the pantheons to suit them. And although First Edition did drive me bonkers with how Loa were handled, I did appreciate that the books themselves encouraged changing things to suit your tastes, something that I haven't seen as much with their other lines (like Werewolf or Changeling - or maybe I didn't see the references? Not sure). For me, that was a lot of the fun, coming up with changes to the pantheons, writing new PSPs, tweaking rules.<br /> <br /> So I, for one, am also very hopeful for any definitive guidelines on what it takes to build a rocking pantheon of your own. Tips and advice to help me improve the pantheons I've written for my own games would be fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2789-laume78","name":"laume78","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T21:28:57-07:00","id":249459,"title":"","content":"So, I've come back from a long time not posting on this board and I want to comment on something mentioned<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=233619#post233619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Zeus, Jupiter and Tinia </span></span>are all the same god, but that god may be mantling different dots of Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.... sets a terrifying precedent for me. One of the things I wasn't fond of about Scion 1e was that it mixed the Aztec, Maya, and other Mesoamerican cultures into a single slurry. 1e Hero gave us the AKAs that ranged understandable(most scholars believe that Guetzalcoatl, Kukulcan, and Gukumatz are all the same god spread across various times and a vast geography), to the utterly wrong (No, Tezcatlipoca is not Tohil, anyone who tried to imply that to an expert on Mesoamerica would be trowel-smacked). Then, it just went nuts, particularly with making the Aztec antagonist Huracan, a god found only in Maya mythology, separated by about as much distance as Greece is from Norway.... <br /> <br /> The point I'm trying to make is that I really hope this isn't used to make a single &quot;Mayincatec&quot; group of gods. We've got plenty of that across pop culture, we don't need another entry for the list...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T04:22:29-07:00","id":249687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=249459#post249459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've come back from a long time not posting on this board and I want to comment on something mentioned<br /> This.... sets a terrifying precedent for me. One of the things I wasn't fond of about Scion 1e was that it mixed the Aztec, Maya, and other Mesoamerican cultures into a single slurry. 1e Hero gave us the AKAs that ranged understandable(most scholars believe that Guetzalcoatl, Kukulcan, and Gukumatz are all the same god spread across various times and a vast geography), to the utterly wrong (No, Tezcatlipoca is not Tohil, anyone who tried to imply that to an expert on Mesoamerica would be trowel-smacked). Then, it just went nuts, particularly with making the Aztec antagonist Huracan, a god found only in Maya mythology, separated by about as much distance as Greece is from Norway....<br /> <br /> The point I'm trying to make is that I really hope this isn't used to make a single &quot;Mayincatec&quot; group of gods. We've got plenty of that across pop culture, we don't need another entry for the list...</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like the idea of gods taking on mantles to distinguish themselves, I also enjoy the idea of divine politics between similiar pantheons. Hopefully, this will be written in a suggestive way (he he) that Zeus might have taken on the mantle of xxx, yyy and zzz if they don't exist in your games as a separate pantheon.<br /> <br /> or even better...<br /> <br /> Two similiar gods (Jupiter and Zeus) take on the mantle of eachother... and get caught red handed... DUN DUN DUN<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T04:23:15-07:00","id":249688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=249459#post249459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've come back from a long time not posting on this board and I want to comment on something mentioned</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, knowing how passionate you are about those pantheon, I hope they get a really good write up in the next Scion game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T06:39:07-07:00","id":249733,"title":"","content":"I know that mentioning the Percy Jackson series is a good way to get smacked, but the Heroes of Olympus series at least has made a pretty decent attempt at the whole 'same god in a different mantle' thing. The differences between Hera as Hera and Hera as Juno (not to mention the Ares and Mars differences also) were pretty cool.<br /> <br /> I could see the mantle thing working with what is clearly the same deity at a different point, so I'm hoping that it also doesn't lapse into just lumping similar (depending on how you squint and look at them) gods all into one bundle. I would hate to think of lumping Coyote, the Monkey King and Loki together as mantles of the same Trickster God template. That would suck badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T06:45:00-07:00","id":249745,"title":"","content":"I suspect the focus is mainly going to be on neighboring pantheons, where real-world cultural borrowing resulted in the same god (or a minor variation thereof) appearing in multiple Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T06:50:08-07:00","id":249750,"title":"","content":"Joseph Campbell ruined a lot of things with his &quot;Masks of God&quot; stuff.<br /> And Percy Jackson should get you smacked.<br /> I'd be willing to bet a whole dime that Jim Butcher's latest book and his take on Hades was a criticism against Riordan's rather inane view on that deity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T07:36:26-07:00","id":249799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=249750#post249750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Percy Jackson should get you smacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>on this I disagree. Most of my players has read and throughly enjoyed the Percy Jacksson series. They've specificly asked me to run games more like them (which is difficult seeing how I haven't read them). The movies gave me a pretty scion-esque feel though, so I can really see why people would like a game like that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T08:13:49-07:00","id":249833,"title":"","content":"*shrugs*<br /> If they enjoyed Percy Jackson then the reality of the myths...(heh) must be damn disappointing. After all, Poseidon was one of the biggest dicks in the myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T08:28:32-07:00","id":249837,"title":"","content":"Meh. Each to their own. They're an entertaining series of books, accuracy aside. Although, really, which Greek god wasn't a dick at some point? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T08:35:56-07:00","id":249839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point I'm trying to make is that I really hope this isn't used to make a single &quot;Mayincatec&quot; group of gods. We've got plenty of that across pop culture, we don't need another entry for the list... </div> </div> </div>Quetzacoatl, Kukulcan, and Gukumatz are good examples of what I'm talking about; I'll include them with the three slightly-better-known Etruscan-Greco-Roman gods who are the same god. <br /> <br /> The Aztec, Incan and Mayan pantheons are well-known to be very different. The Titans themselves have also changed (and aren't necessarily present in all settings anyways).<br /> <br /> I know you've got a personal stake in this, so take my reassurance that we've done our homework on American pantheons of all stripes and locales, North and South. When we say the Aztec pantheon is returning for the Hero core, we do mean the actual Aztecs, not a less diverse Mesoamerican one. If Huracan doesn't like an Aztec Scion, it's because he thinks Mexico City doesn't deserve the title of tollan and is sore about Chichen Itza (that is an off-the-cuff example; I'm not writing those pantheons). Keep in mind, though, that our foremost goal is a playable and enjoyable mythological game allowing players to embody the myths of legend, wear divine mantles of succession and create their own myths in the vein of old in the modern day whilst being a badass, not arguing about who's God K and who isn't. Accuracy and respect are still very, very high priorities. But if we're looking at Lugh of the Tuatha de Dannen and see the Welsh Lleu Llaw Gyffes and Lugus of the Gauls, there's a judgment call to be made.<br /> <br /> As for Tohil, Tezcatlipoca and Huracan all having something to do with leadership and a screwy leg, see my comment before re: Zeus, Indra, and Perun not being the same god but occupying a similar role and possessing some similar characteristics.<br /> <br /> Hope that's a bit reassuring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 09-05-2014, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T13:59:52-07:00","id":250106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=249839#post249839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hope that's a bit reassuring.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. It really is. And I understand that as a game of being a mythological badass, some things are going to be less-than scholarly, but I appreciate the effort, and just this post has me more optimistic about it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=249839#post249839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Tohil, Tezcatlipoca and Huracan all having something to do with leadership and a screwy leg, see my comment before re: Zeus, Indra, and Perun not being the same god but occupying a similar role and possessing some similar characteristics.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually interesting, because according to my translation of the Popol Vuh, Tohil is actually an aspect of Huracan. Perhaps a better example would be Tlaloc, Chaac, and Cocijo, who are made one dude in Scion 1e, but who were worshiped as different entities (Tlaloc symbols appear in Maya hieroglyphs, where Chaac is also present, Cocijo vessels are found in excavations of the Zapotec area of Teotihuacan, where Tlaloc was one of, if not the head god) despite having a lot of similarities (rain gods with goggle eyes and snakey bits). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T06:08:22-07:00","id":262085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ebon Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=242279#post242279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall - Can you estimate when you (or someone, anyone, else of the team) can spill some concrete mechanics? I mean you hinted at the very general function of the system, but i am really curious about it in a much deeper way...i would want to see examples of mechanics at work etc. .<br /> Scion 2 is one of my most anticipated games.<br /> <br /> Thanks for doing this, btw. Answers from the people involved is always a nice thing to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to quote myself in the hope that Neall will see it this time around. The mechanical side is very important to me and will most probably be the deciding factor if i buy into Scion 2nd Ed. or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/153-ebon-wolf","name":"Ebon Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T08:52:21-07:00","id":262201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ebon Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=262085#post262085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to quote myself in the hope that Neall will see it this time around. The mechanical side is very important to me and will most probably be the deciding factor if i buy into Scion 2nd Ed. or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core system for use in Scion and Trinity will be submitted for Open Development, so you'll be able to comment on it directly. It'll be a spill like an oil tanker explosion - you'Il get the entire basic core system (mostly) at once, sans one or two bits for fine-tuning.<br /> <br /> I quoted October at Rich Thomas during the GenCon panel, but it's looking a little later than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T10:52:56-07:00","id":264681,"title":"","content":"That's very cool! Thanks for the heads-up, Neall. I look forward to the open development phase...i really hope it will not be too many days past October <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/153-ebon-wolf","name":"Ebon Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T15:09:09-07:00","id":264906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=249733#post249733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that mentioning the Percy Jackson series is a good way to get smacked-</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why this would be the case. It's a good series and does a very good job with it's mythology given what it has to do.<br /> <br /> Blood of Olympus is going to be <i>epic</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T15:30:51-07:00","id":264918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=264906#post264906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why this would be the case. It's a good series and does a very good job with it's mythology given what it has to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<i>eeeeeeeeehhh</i>. I thought the first book was pretty mediocre, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T15:32:02-07:00","id":264919,"title":"","content":"Because if Percy Jackson is scrutinized even a little against the actual myth, it really does come across as pretty lame to me. And all I have to do is point at the first movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T16:51:21-07:00","id":266510,"title":"","content":"Hmf...it's the books that I found crappy. I only read the first book, but after going through my old Greek myth stuff, I'm having a difficult time imagining anyone that appreciates and likes the old myths...liking any of these books, which were...well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:19:13-07:00","id":266521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=266510#post266510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmf...it's the books that I found crappy. I only read the first book, but after going through my old Greek myth stuff, I'm having a difficult time imagining anyone that appreciates and likes the old myths...liking any of these books, which were...well...</div> </div> </div> </div>I adore Greek Mythology. it's what triggered my passion when I was eight years old, and I've also read the Percy Jackson books. They are a relatively good set of YA books that take the mythology and give it fresh twists. Are they perfect? No, nowhere near it, but they're fun popcorn reads that encourage further reading of the tropes and myths within each story.<br /> <br /> So here, a person who loves Greek myths and reads the PJ books and enjoys them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:57:14-07:00","id":266533,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* They were NOT written as YA...more like pre-pubescent. Poseidon was among the worst gods when it came to violence. He rapes Medusa (Athena's priestess) in Athena's temple and Athena doles out the wrath on Medusa since she's helpless to do much anything against Poseidon himself...Hades, the one major god that just happens to be the most dutiful if not genuinely fair, becomes the devil...and they mention &quot;Hercules...? Really? I thought his name was &quot;Heracles.&quot;..there's just a laundry list against this series. And I just find it laughable that here, in this forum, that so bitterly whines, bitches and moans over accuracy over a game, does little griping over these books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T18:11:05-07:00","id":266540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=266533#post266533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* They were NOT written as YA...more like pre-pubescent. Poseidon was among the worst gods when it came to violence. He rapes Medusa (Athena's priestess) in Athena's temple and Athena doles out the wrath on Medusa since she's helpless to do much anything against Poseidon himself...Hades, the one major god that just happens to be the most dutiful if not genuinely fair, becomes the devil...and they mention &quot;Hercules...? Really? I thought his name was &quot;Heracles.&quot;..there's just a laundry list against this series. And I just find it laughable that here, in this forum, that so bitterly whines, bitches and moans over accuracy over a game, does little griping over these books.</div> </div> </div> </div>YA covers a wide range of ages in both the audience and the protagnosists of the books themselves. Percy Jackson, being twelve at the beginning of the series, is definitely reaching into the YA levels but I digress...<br /> <br /> Yes, the Greek Myths are unapologetically horrific in terms of what was deemed acceptable culturally and socially. What were stories of ordinary deeds and punishments of yesteryear are terrible crimes of today. I don't think anyone in this forum, including myself, sees that any different. And before you deliberately flame-bait, you have no idea what I discuss outside of this forum so I can't show you the dozen page essasies I've written about the series depicting the inaccuraies and ways the books differ from the myths.<br /> <br /> Moving on again. Percy Jackson updates the myths and never claims to be historically accurate. RR has taken the myths into his own universe where Cherion never dies, the Underworlds are a strange metaphysical place, and there's a masquerade. They're also designed for YA and I can tell you that most &quot;children&quot; tales of Greek mythology definitely leave out the nastier bits. It's bowdlerizing in the same way most stories are for younger readers. <br /> <br /> It's fine if you don't like them, they're not for everyone; but they can be enjoyed as popcorn fluff the same way I can watch medical shows and watch every procedure being done wrong without freaking out at that moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T19:44:50-07:00","id":266571,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* I already said it's the books I found crappy...You want to nitpick? I can nitpick. But nitpicking doesn't change my opinion. Hey, I understand that others enjoyed the books. I get that. They wouldn't be popular otherwise. But no argument, or logic, or whatever, can make me like something I didn't like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T20:29:56-07:00","id":266580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=266571#post266571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* I already said it's the books I found crappy...You want to nitpick? I can nitpick. But nitpicking doesn't change my opinion. Hey, I understand that others enjoyed the books. I get that. They wouldn't be popular otherwise. But no argument, or logic, or whatever, can make me like something I didn't like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No one's expecting to change your mind, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T16:26:08-07:00","id":267043,"title":"","content":"Please try not to derail the thread with critiques of Percy Jackson. Take it to Off Topic or, if you have a way to tie it to the game, a new thread here under Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T08:19:15-08:00","id":326020,"title":"","content":"Any news on when the open development will hit? When can we get a peek at the new Scion rulessystem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/153-ebon-wolf","name":"Ebon Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T11:52:16-08:00","id":326180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ebon Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=326020#post326020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any news on when the open development will hit? When can we get a peek at the new Scion rulessystem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Within the new year (January 2015), I'm pretty confident. At least, the new iteration should hit internal testing 'round Christmas.<br /> <br /> It keeps getting pushed back more and more, I know. But <i>this </i>time...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T04:53:53-08:00","id":326847,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Neall! In that case i'll keep my fingers crossed for a release in January 15.<br /> If you feel like it, keep us posted on how the internal playtesting around Christmas is going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/153-ebon-wolf","name":"Ebon Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T13:19:00-08:00","id":327349,"title":"","content":"I'll have my fingers crossed. We've just started up a Scion game here--like, two sessions in and the next one's going to be a few weeks yet for assorted holiday-related reasons--and while I'm the only one of us to frequent this site, it'd be kind of cool if I could get other people on board with taking a closer look at it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T00:50:12-08:00","id":328982,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to this, I'm waiting for <i>any </i>information on Scion 2e and Exalted 3e for my group. We enjoyed Scion, but I'm really wanting to see what you'll do with 2e, and so far it sounds damn interesting. Any news you're moving forward is good news.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T07:05:47-08:00","id":329181,"title":"","content":"As a side note--and I think I've mentioned it somewhere but I can't find it now, so it might have been on the old forums and I think it bears repeating--I'm kind of hoping that we don't see a return of the Long Road to Heaven or the like. I ran numbers at one point and IIRC it was roughly a full sourcebook's worth of material spread throughout three books, and I never even bothered with it. The only thing I spent more than a five-second cursory glance at was the evolution of the characters through the tiers (which I thought was really cool!) but the massive space spent upon a pre-structured chronicle was almost entirely wasted upon me, and I don't know if I've ever heard of anyone using it or mining it. <br /> <br /> I'm going to hurl my wallet at the screen the moment the option presents itself regardless, but I'm really hoping the wordcount is better spent next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T11:17:29-08:00","id":329429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=329181#post329181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to hurl my wallet at the screen the moment the option presents itself regardless, but I'm really hoping the wordcount is better spent next time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You and me both. My throwing arm has been cocked and ready for months now, just twitching to let loose.<br /> <br /> That said, I didn't even bother reading the Long Road to Heaven all the way through, and I've had the books for years now. I just couldn't get through it. I just could not bring myself to particularly care about the characters enough to finish finding out what they were going through. My only interest was in what my group's characters were doing and the thematic information about the universe in which they were playing.<br /> <br /> For those GMs who are crunching for time and could really do with some preconceived stories to run, I'm sure the Long Road to Heaven would be vastly useful, but I'd personally rather see that sort of content packaged separately and sold as stand-alone adventure books like I've seen many other RPG lines do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2789-laume78","name":"laume78","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:35:06-08:00","id":424143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=326180#post326180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Within the new year (January 2015), I'm pretty confident. At least, the new iteration should hit internal testing 'round Christmas.<br /> <br /> It keeps getting pushed back more and more, I know. But <i>this </i>time...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was wondering what the status of the open development for Scion 2e is. Any news you can/want to share, Neall?<br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/153-ebon-wolf","name":"Ebon Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:55:59-08:00","id":424266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ebon Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/232426-gencon-panel?p=424143#post424143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was wondering what the status of the open development for Scion 2e is. Any news you can/want to share, Neall?<br /> Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second drafts. Had a couple of funky results from the playtests. Then, it'll go to internal development again, and then - finally - to open dev.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:02:22-08:00","id":425429,"title":"","content":"*Bumping for a liiittle bit